  "claim_boundary": "DIRAC-015 completes the conditional free-Dirac continuum derivation. DIRAC-016--025 add scoped copy, spin, transport, clock, zitterbewegung and velocity identities, including continuous-angle Hamiltonian covariance. The chain does not classify arbitrary nonlocal or flavor-mixing roots, prove a uniform fixed-physical-time convergence rate, or prove localized electron transport. A pure branch's global phase is not claimed to be an observable clock. The chain does not establish a localized nonlinear native electron trajectory, an exact finite-spacing phase-harmony law, or a classical hidden light-speed path. Temporal and spatial generators remain distinct. DIRAC-026 derives free Lorentz boosts; DIRAC-027 derives the Pauli--Lubanski spin-half invariant; DIRAC-028 derives the infinitesimal Wigner--Thomas half factor; DIRAC-029 derives free charge conjugation; DIRAC-030 derives the free Gordon current split. These do not establish exact finite-spacing Lorentz invariance, electric charge or interacting positrons, electromagnetic coupling, magnetic moment or g-factor, SI calibration, electron formation, or canonical LFM status."
